data: {"response":{"background":false,"completed_at":1791536179,"created_at":1791536179,"error":null,"frequency_penalty":0,"id":"resp_814922","incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"max_output_tokens":null,"max_tool_calls":null,"metadata":{},"model":"gpt-oss:120b","object":"response","output":[{"encrypted_content":"The tool is named exec_command not apply_patch. Need to use exec_command with `apply_patch`? Actually there is no apply_patch tool; we use `git apply`? We can use `apply_patch` as part of repository? The environment may support `apply_patch` command via `apply_patch` tool? Not defined. Use `apply_patch` command via exec? In previous interactions, I've used `apply_patch` tool? Not listed. There's only exec_command, write_stdin, request_user_input, view_image, get_goal, create_goal, update_goal. So we need to modify files via shell commands like `apply_patch`? Usually we can use `apply_patch` by invoking `apply_patch` function? Not defined. Might use `git apply` with a patch. Simpler: rewrite server.js completely.\n\nWe'll overwrite server.js with new content.\n\n","id":"rs_265153","summary":[{"text":"The tool is named exec_command not apply_patch. Need to use exec_command with `apply_patch`? Actually there is no apply_patch tool; we use `git apply`? We can use `apply_patch` as part of repository? The environment may support `apply_patch` command via `apply_patch` tool? Not defined. Use `apply_patch` command via exec? In previous interactions, I've used `apply_patch` tool? Not listed. There's only exec_command, write_stdin, request_user_input, view_image, get_goal, create_goal, update_goal. So we need to modify files via shell commands like `apply_patch`? Usually we can use `apply_patch` by invoking `apply_patch` function? Not defined. Might use `git apply` with a patch. Simpler: rewrite server.js completely.\n\nWe'll overwrite server.js with new content.\n\n","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"arguments":"{\"cmd\":\"cat \\u003e server.js 